{"base_rate":0.43478260869565216,"brier":0.19124249011857708,"bss":0.22179017482517482,"bss_hi":0.31899014030307277,"bss_lo":0.09377914349924048,"chart":{"base":[625.8,65.5],"fp":[263.9,267.1],"lead":"62,239.9 272,214.4 482,167.4 692,124.2","note":{"base":"skill 0.22 — higher than 31% of cities","fp":"low end +6pp, high end +23pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 36% of cities","rel":"promised 6% → rained 12%; promised 97% → rained 75%"},"rel":"100.1,412 424,283.9 672.1,144.1"},"country":"LV","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve"],"ece":0.14638339920948623,"ess":335.48796498905966,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Riga</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Riga rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>76%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>9%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 506 days, 2024-04-27 to\n2026-02-08. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 8.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.22, ranked 146 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(91&ndash;173) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>150</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>21%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>50</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>44%</td><td class='num'><b>39%</b></td><td class='num'>49</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>69%</td><td class='num'><b>45%</b></td><td class='num'>53</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>68%</b></td><td class='num'>47</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>76%</b></td><td class='num'>157</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Riga</b> <span class=\"muted\">Latvia</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.22</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>91&ndash;173\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>506 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Riga &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Riga\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line clas